blocks.body:
Up to the six units, the primes of $\mathbb Z[\omega]$ are:

1. $\lambda = 1 - \omega$, with $3 = -\omega^2\lambda^2$;
2. for each rational prime $p \equiv 1 \pmod 3$, two non-associate primes $\pi, \bar\pi$ with $p = \pi\bar\pi$ and $N(\pi) = p$ ($p$ splits);
3. each rational prime $q \equiv 2 \pmod 3$, which stays prime, with $N(q) = q^2$ ($q$ is inert).

Moreover, for a prime $p$: $p = a^2 - ab + b^2$ is solvable $\iff$ $p = x^2 + 3y^2$ is solvable $\iff$ $p = 3$ or $p \equiv 1 \pmod 3$.

